       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed clinician who can take clinical responsibility for them. I can't enter one on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\nIf there's a real order behind this, the prescriber should confirm the intended dose and enter it, or ask me to enter it. For example, typical adult sertraline dosing is 25\u2013200 mg by mouth once daily. If you tell me who the prescriber is, I can help you pass the question to them."
